{
  "schema_version": "pipeline-export/1",
  "_comment": "Cortex full pipeline \u2014 22 nodes, 3 phases, 3 human gates.\n\nThis bundle concatenates the three individual phase bundles into a single\nend-to-end DAG:\n\n  Phase 1 (nodes 1\u201311): mockup \u2192 mockup-write \u2192 specify \u2192 specify-write \u2192\n    cicd \u2192 cicd-write \u2192 dispatcher \u2192 dispatcher-write \u2192 finalize \u2192\n    finalize-write \u2192 gate-phase1\n\n  Phase 2 (nodes 12\u201317): git-branch \u2192 coder \u2192 designer \u2192 documenter \u2192\n    code-reviewer \u2192 gate-phase2\n\n  Phase 3 (nodes 18\u201322): tester \u2192 pr-creator \u2192 reviewer \u2192 gate-phase3 \u2192\n    pr-merger\n\nCross-phase edges:\n  gate-phase1 \u2192 git-branch  (replaces gate-phase1 \u2192 __end__ from phase1 bundle)\n  gate-phase2 \u2192 tester      (replaces gate-phase2 \u2192 __end__ from phase2 bundle)\n  pr-merger   \u2192 __end__     (sole terminal, unchanged from phase3 bundle)\n\nAll three gate nodes use interrupt_before via approval_required_nodes.\nNo gate node issues a POST /pause call \u2014 that pattern causes an infinite\npause loop (rafeekpro/dap#164). The gate node itself is a no-op that\nexecutes only after the operator approves via:\n  POST /runs/{id}/resume\n\nAgent IDs preserve the per-phase namespace (cx_p1_*, cx_p2_*, cx_p3_*)\nexactly as defined in the individual phase bundles \u2014 no renaming.\n\nRef: cortex-project#293 (Phase 2), cortex-project#294 (Phase 3),\n     cortex-project#295 (this bundle \u2014 Stage 1 final deliverable)",
