  "install_instructions": {
    "summary": "Import this bundle into a DAP engine that has cortex-project installed.",
    "steps": [
      "1. Ensure cortex-project is installed in the DAP engine venv: uv add --path /path/to/cortex-project",
      "2. Set CORTEX_ env vars (GH_TOKEN_READ, GH_TOKEN_ISSUES, GH_TOKEN_CODE, GH_TOKEN_MERGE, DATABASE_URL)",
      "3. Strip _comment and install_instructions before importing: POST /pipelines/import with {schema_version, pipeline, bundled_agents}",
      "4. Create a run: POST /runs with pipeline_id and initial_state.extensions={issue_url, issue_number, repo, workspace_path, ...}",
      "5. Phase 1 runs automatically (mockup \u2192 finalize, each followed by a write node updating the GitHub issue)",
      "6. Run pauses at gate-phase1 \u2014 approve: POST /runs/{id}/resume",
      "7. Phase 2 starts (git-branch \u2192 coder \u2192 designer \u2192 documenter \u2192 code-reviewer); code-reviewer may retry up to 2 times",
      "8. Run pauses at gate-phase2 \u2014 approve: POST /runs/{id}/resume",
      "9. Phase 3 starts (tester \u2192 pr-creator \u2192 reviewer); run pauses at gate-phase3",
      "10. Approve: POST /runs/{id}/resume",
      "11. pr-merger merges the PR using GH_TOKEN_MERGE (rlagowski \u2014 separate user from code authors)"
    ],
    "env_vars": [
      "CORTEX_GH_TOKEN_READ=ghp_...",
      "CORTEX_GH_TOKEN_ISSUES=ghp_...",
      "CORTEX_GH_TOKEN_CODE=ghp_...",
      "CORTEX_GH_TOKEN_MERGE=ghp_...",
      "CORTEX_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cortex_project:...@host:5432/cortex_project"
    ],
    "gate_design": "All three gates (gate-phase1, gate-phase2, gate-phase3) use interrupt_before via approval_required_nodes \u2014 NOT python-func calls to POST /pause. This avoids the infinite pause loop described in rafeekpro/dap#164. Each gate node is a no-op (cortex.dap_steps.human_gate:noop) that executes only after the operator approves."
  }
}